   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as the SMILES below. I did not run it through a parser, so the validity check was done by hand.\n\n- **Glutarimide:** a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl ring is attached through its C3 to the isoindolinone nitrogen. This carbon has plain bonds, so I gave it no stereo.\n- **Isoindolinone:** the lactam C=O sits on the aromatic carbon next to the CH2-bearing carbon. The alkyne is on the aromatic carbon adjacent to the CH2-bearing carbon.\n- **Linker:** an alkyne followed by five CH2 groups and then a C(=O) amide, which acylates the ring nitrogen of the bicyclic core.\n- **Bicyclic core:** an eight-membered ring (N, CH2, CH2, CH, N, C=O, CH, CH2) fused to a pyrrolidine through the CH and the N.\n  - The fusion CH carries a wedge to the CH2 above it.\n  - The pyrrolidine CH carries a wedge to its carboxamide.\n  - The ring CH next to the lactam carbonyl carries a wedge to its NH.\n- **Side chain:** the amide NH leads to a stereocentre (wedge to CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O)NH2) bearing a 5-phenylthiazol-2-yl group.\n- **Benzothiophene:** the 2-carboxamide is on the thiophene ring, and a CF2\u2013PO3H2 group is on C5 of the benzo ring.\n\nI assigned @/@@ at the four wedged centres from the wedge geometry, taking the implicit hydrogen as pointing away from the viewer.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(C(=O)N1)N1Cc2c(C1=O)cccc2C#CCCCCCC(=O)N1CC[C@H]3CC[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](COC(N)=O)c4ncc(-c5ccccc5)s4)N3C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)c3cc4cc(C(F)(F)P(=O)(O)O)ccc4s3)C1"
